# Robot corpus rules

1. Never count fixed joints, gripper joints, finger joints, or sensor frames as arm DOF.
2. Use the explicit base-to-tip chain in `data/robot_corpus/manifest.json`.
3. Treat Fetch as the arm-only `torso_lift_link -> wrist_roll_link` subchain.
4. Do not convert a 7R control into a 6R robot by deleting an arbitrary joint.
5. Keep raw third-party sources unmodified under `third_party/robot_corpus/`.
6. Record the resolved Git commit before deriving normalized kinematic data.
7. Do not redistribute meshes until the exact snapshot license has been reviewed.
8. A Xacro entry point is not a flat URDF; expansion failures must be reported, not bypassed.
9. Preserve joint axes and origins exactly before attempting symmetry detection.
10. Project planar fixtures must be regenerated from `planar3r_instances.json`, never hand-edited.
